The magnitude is perceptually more significant than the phase; and should therefore be quantized first. Furthermore, if the phase were quantized first, the very limited bit allocation available for the phase would lead to an excessively degraded spectral matching of the magnitude in favor of a 

somewhat improved, but less important, matching of the waveform. For the above distortion, the quantized phase vector is given by: = argmin { (r - e* |r

